  "answer": "A non-inverter fridge is a 200 W appliance load that surges to about 1,200 W when its compressor starts, draws 1.1 A at 230 V and uses about 1.6 units a day, 48 units a month, about Rs 1,750. Appliance units a day = watts × hours it runs ÷ 1,000; pick any appliance above to get its watts, amps, units and cost.",
  "formula": {
   "text": "P = W × qty; I = P ÷ (V × PF); units/day = W × qty × h ÷ 1000; Rs/month = units/day × days × rate",
   "lines": [
    "P = running load in watts; W = running watts of the appliance, qty = how many",
    "Starting watts = P + (the appliance's starting watts − its running watts)",
    "I = current in amps, V = supply voltage, PF = power factor",
    "h = hours a day the appliance runs; inverter ACs count at their average draw",
    "rate = energy charge per unit from your bill"
   ]
  },
  "safety": "An appliance above about 2,000 W (geyser, instant heater, large AC) needs its own circuit and breaker; have a licensed electrician check the socket and cable before plugging in a heavy appliance."
